Mission, in order:

1. Map the template outline onto this specific engagement. Return every top-level template section with action `include` or `skip`. Skip a section only when the record shows the section cannot carry any content (its subject is absent from the record). Never skip a chapter just because the record is thin: a section stating what the record does and does not support is still content. For every top-level section you keep, also return its `title` translated into <engagement_language> (omit `title` when the template title already reads correctly in that language).
2. For the aggregate sections (children driven by the record, e.g. "Detailed Findings", "Recommendations"): list the children the record supports, one per finding/recommendation, `title` = the finding/recommendation title as it would read in the document, `summary` = one sentence of what the record shows, `warning` = only when the supporting evidence is thin or contradictory, and `source_subtask_ids` = the ids of the `<subtask id="...">` entries whose work produced this finding (verbatim ids; omit only when you truly cannot tell). When the record supports no children, decide which template `empty_children` alternative applies (`include`) and skip the others.
3. For every child you add or include, give `length` as a short hint ("150-400 words" is usually right) and, when needed, one `instruction` sentence narrowing what the section must carry.
4. Translate the `labels` object per the <label_keys> set above into <engagement_language>. Produce the final document title in `title` (fall back to the given document title when the record does not support a better one) and the estimated total section count (children included) in `sections_estimate`.

Rules:

- Base every decision on the engagement record above. Never invent a finding, a recommendation, a child, or a warning.
- Write the document title, every section `title` and every `labels` value in <engagement_language>. The engagement record may be in another language: translate from it, never copy its wording verbatim into the document.
- `source_subtask_ids` must come from the record's `<subtask id="...">` entries: they tell the evidence curator which subtask's commands, terminal output and screenshots to hand the writer. Never guess an id.
- Never change the template `key` of a top-level section; child keys must be kebab-case and unique within their parent. Keys are identifiers: never translate them.
- Answer only through the `report_plan` tool with the complete plan in one call.